WEBVTT

00:04.540 --> 00:11.040
This is an ancint lullaby whose origins are unknown and whose exact original meaning has been lost

00:04.540 --> 00:08.080
Sleep now, sleep.

00:08.080 --> 00:11.040
I will protect you.

00:47.130 --> 00:55.900
(Wanting you to just be near,
to feel your breath upon my ear)

00:55.940 --> 01:04.940
(Wishing you would call my name,
'Cause only you can light the flame)

01:04.980 --> 01:11.710
Constantly searching,
still can't find

01:14.320 --> 01:20.390
Ever illusive peace of mind

01:22.560 --> 01:31.130
Sometimes it's near,
but slips away

01:31.170 --> 01:37.770
And I'm faced with another day

01:38.980 --> 01:44.710
Of wanting you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:44.750 --> 01:49.050
...to just be near
('Cause only you can light the flame)

01:49.090 --> 01:53.530
Of wishing you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:53.560 --> 01:57.960
...would call my name,
to feel your breath upon my ear

01:58.000 --> 02:02.490
Of wanting you... wishing you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

02:02.540 --> 02:10.380
Call my name, 'cause only
you can light the flame

02:15.530 --> 02:19.660
Willow Woman

02:23.410 --> 02:25.990
Don't get too close to us for your own good...

02:28.790 --> 02:31.870
I can't believe you just dozed off like that!

02:33.290 --> 02:36.290
I've been waiting for so long that my tea's gotten cold...

02:37.210 --> 02:41.170
I would expect no less from the man who handed over his inheritance,

02:41.170 --> 02:44.220
one of the finest candle shops in Edo, to the
head clerk and then left the business!

02:44.220 --> 02:47.430
You've got a lot of nerve, don't you?

02:47.470 --> 02:50.680
Well... I'm just terrible at business...

02:50.980 --> 02:53.270
It's not that I have a lot of nerve. Please don't embarrass me--

02:53.020 --> 02:54.350
I'm not praising you!

02:54.650 --> 02:55.190
Thought so.

02:55.730 --> 02:57.770
More importantly, what is this?!

02:58.030 --> 03:01.400
You haven't written one word; no, not even one letter!

03:01.450 --> 03:02.990
Well, I just haven't been---

03:02.990 --> 03:04.450
Haven't been inspired?

03:05.570 --> 03:08.370
[Note: This is a sarcasm since "sensei" is a title that is only given to well-respected writers.]

03:05.570 --> 03:06.910
Oh, excuse me, great sensei!

03:06.910 --> 03:08.370
Are you tired?

03:08.870 --> 03:12.200
If so, then why don't you write down a riddle or two?

03:12.330 --> 03:14.870
Don't say such mean things...

03:14.460 --> 03:15.670
Sensei!

03:16.210 --> 03:22.130
I'm not asking you to write a master work or something
that'll be performed in some theater!

03:22.800 --> 03:26.180
I just want some riddles for children!

03:26.340 --> 03:27.850
"Can't get inspiration..."?  Heh.

03:27.970 --> 03:32.770
It's a hundred years too early for you to be rattling
off lines as if you were an accomplished writer.

03:33.350 --> 03:34.060
Sorry.

03:33.370 --> 03:36.060
Before you apologize, write something for me!

03:36.730 --> 03:39.190
It's just that when I try to think of something to write...

03:41.110 --> 03:42.400
Don't come near me!

03:43.490 --> 03:44.610
Wh-Wh-What's the matter?

03:45.990 --> 03:47.700
I-I'm sorry.

03:48.410 --> 03:49.910
But really...

03:49.910 --> 03:51.660
Rather than write riddles,

03:51.660 --> 03:54.750
I've been thinking I'd like to write a book of 100 stories...

03:54.870 --> 03:56.330
A book of 100 stories?

03:56.380 --> 03:59.000
Not that empty dream of yours again...

04:00.380 --> 04:01.960
I'm serious!

04:03.800 --> 04:06.090
Okay, okay... 100 stories it is then.

04:06.430 --> 04:09.140
Why don't you go to Yanagiya then?

04:09.350 --> 04:11.350
Yanagiya? That inn?

04:11.850 --> 04:12.810
That's right.

04:12.810 --> 04:16.560
Ten years ago, the bride and baby of the inn's master Kichibee-san,

04:16.560 --> 04:19.520
died mysterious deaths under the yanagi!

04:19.560 --> 04:22.110
It was said to be the doing of a Yanagi Onna, wasn't it?

04:22.190 --> 04:23.440
"Yanagi Onna"?

04:23.740 --> 04:29.200
[Note: Yanagi means willow.]

04:23.740 --> 04:29.200
It's the spirit of a large yanagi in the inn's inner gardens; it is the inn's namesake.

04:31.080 --> 04:36.160
Apparently, the shop has been protected by a Yanagi Onna for generations,

04:36.160 --> 04:39.750
but the Yanagi Onna fell in love with Kichibee-san

04:39.750 --> 04:43.090
and has killed all of his brides out of jealousy.

04:45.050 --> 04:47.470
The yanagi's spirit was jealous, huh?

04:47.470 --> 04:50.430
Then the new bride may be in danger, too.

04:50.680 --> 04:53.640
What? There's a new bride?

04:53.720 --> 04:56.350
Yes, the wedding celebration should be today.

04:56.560 --> 04:57.810
What did you say?!

05:06.990 --> 05:09.780
I wonder if I should look for a new writer...

05:19.080 --> 05:21.290
Congratulations on your wedding.

05:21.670 --> 05:23.590
The weather's nice today, too.

05:33.640 --> 05:34.890
Four of them.

05:34.890 --> 05:36.560
There have been four dead brides.

05:36.560 --> 05:38.770
There have been four dead babies, too.

05:39.190 --> 05:41.400
That's a bit too much of a coincidence.

05:42.310 --> 05:43.650
That's right.

05:48.070 --> 05:49.400
Excuse me!

05:50.860 --> 05:53.870
Allow me to clear your table...

05:54.700 --> 05:56.950
My, my... these are good.

06:00.710 --> 06:01.920
Hey, are you with Yanagiya?

06:02.670 --> 06:03.880
What? Well, yes...

06:04.540 --> 06:07.800
Say, a new bride has come, hasn't she?

06:07.840 --> 06:10.090
There's that rumor... will she be okay?

06:10.760 --> 06:12.130
What rumor?

06:12.430 --> 06:15.510
Don't be so coy... I'm talking about the Yanagi Onna rumor!

06:19.560 --> 06:22.770
Hey, you! You're a fuda-selling monk, aren't you?

06:24.060 --> 06:27.190
Are the rumors about that place across the street really true?

06:27.900 --> 06:28.900
Er, no...

06:28.900 --> 06:31.950
Are you going to seal the mononoke with those fuda?

06:32.950 --> 06:33.700
Miser.

06:34.450 --> 06:37.830
Anyway, if you're going to talk about mononoke,

06:37.830 --> 06:40.580
you'd be better off talking about Kichibee-san's relatives!

06:41.460 --> 06:45.170
You see, Kichibee-san said that he doesn't need a wife anymore.

06:45.790 --> 06:47.290
You understand, don't you?

06:47.420 --> 06:51.760
His brides keep dying and his relatives keep forcing him to take more.

06:52.260 --> 06:56.930
Really, they just won't think about Kichibee-san's feelings.

06:57.140 --> 06:58.720
Poor man. They just want him to have an heir!

06:59.390 --> 07:00.390
An heir?

07:00.730 --> 07:01.350
Right.

07:01.640 --> 07:04.100
You see, if Kichibee-san doesn't have a child,

07:04.100 --> 07:06.770
then it means that they'll have to choose an heir from the outside.

07:06.900 --> 07:11.150
If that happens, then his relatives won't be able to live off of him anymore!

07:11.860 --> 07:14.910
Oh, perhaps I've said too much.

07:16.120 --> 07:18.870
I'm sorry. Here we go.

07:22.120 --> 07:26.210
In other words, there's always plenty of fodder, to
feed human greed no matter where one may be.

07:26.920 --> 07:30.760
I won't let that girl become a victim of that.

07:31.380 --> 07:32.090
Ogin-san.

07:32.670 --> 07:34.840
You seem quite personally involved this time.

07:35.590 --> 07:37.550
Well, I have my reasons.

07:39.970 --> 07:41.060
What's the matter?

07:41.100 --> 07:42.140
Hey, look.

07:45.310 --> 07:47.400
He doesn't understand yet, does he?

08:05.790 --> 08:08.170
Your bride's quite the pretty one, isn't she?

08:08.170 --> 08:09.500
I'm so happy for you.

08:09.500 --> 08:12.920
I heard that your bride has conceived?

08:13.630 --> 08:16.930
Well done, well done! Congratulations, a thousand congratulations!

08:16.930 --> 08:19.100
With this, Yanagiya's future is safe!

08:35.610 --> 08:36.450
"Congratulations"...

08:39.320 --> 08:41.160
You are mine.

08:44.500 --> 08:46.960
I won't let you be with any other women.

08:48.460 --> 08:52.250
I beg of you! Please don't make me suffer any more.

08:52.460 --> 08:55.050
I am the only one who can protect you.

08:55.090 --> 08:56.880
I live in a different world than you!

08:57.090 --> 08:58.380
We can't be together!

08:58.470 --> 09:00.640
I won't hand you over to another woman!

09:00.680 --> 09:02.640
Yae is pregnant!

09:02.930 --> 09:04.520
I'm not a young man anymore!

09:04.520 --> 09:08.140
If that child isn't born, then this house is finished!

09:08.480 --> 09:09.980
I love you.

09:10.690 --> 09:11.400
You?

09:13.780 --> 09:14.860
Master?

09:16.740 --> 09:17.280
What is it?

09:18.490 --> 09:21.280
Momosuke-san from Ikomaya is here to see you, sir.

09:21.450 --> 09:22.410
Ikomaya?

09:22.450 --> 09:23.780
He is a young man.

09:24.240 --> 09:24.910
Very well.

09:29.830 --> 09:32.210
Congratulations on your wedding!

09:32.500 --> 09:35.630
It's truly the wedding of a great man... so lively!

09:35.920 --> 09:37.510
They're merely making merry.

09:37.630 --> 09:38.260
What?

09:38.970 --> 09:44.010
You turned over your business to your head clerk and retired, didn't you?

09:45.350 --> 09:47.850
I've been terrible at business ever since I was born.

09:48.270 --> 09:52.360
I thought that if I inherited it, then I'd wreck it.

09:52.940 --> 09:55.610
So, I'm currently thinking of becoming a writer.

09:55.730 --> 09:56.980
I'm jealous.

09:57.030 --> 09:59.450
If I had that kind of courage...

09:59.450 --> 10:03.070
No, I'm kind of a hermit...

10:03.580 --> 10:05.910
And why is a "hermit" like you here?

10:08.160 --> 10:09.960
It's about the Yanagi Onna rumors, isn't it?

10:10.130 --> 10:11.430
No...

10:13.340 --> 10:14.380
I'm sorry!

10:14.800 --> 10:16.340
You're an easy person to understand.

10:18.760 --> 10:21.880
Actually... Actually, when I was a kid,

10:21.890 --> 10:27.810
I snuck in here after hearing that a tree spirit called Yanagi Onna was here.

10:56.210 --> 10:58.880
You were probably tricked by the employees.

10:59.510 --> 11:00.800
It had to have been, yes.

11:01.800 --> 11:03.840
There is no Yanagi Onna.

11:04.470 --> 11:05.340
I'm embarrassed.

11:07.600 --> 11:08.930
Oh, thank you.

11:10.730 --> 11:11.480
You're...

11:12.190 --> 11:14.690
Oh, you know one of my employees?

11:15.520 --> 11:16.270
No...

11:16.860 --> 11:18.360
M-Master!

11:19.070 --> 11:21.240
What's wrong? What are you fussing about?

11:22.400 --> 11:23.780
There's a strange man in the garden...

11:32.660 --> 11:34.080
What are you doing?

11:35.210 --> 11:36.830
I'm sorry.

11:37.250 --> 11:41.710
I thought I should seal the mononoke that has possessed your tree.

11:42.220 --> 11:44.260
There is no such thing here.

11:44.430 --> 11:45.470
Please leave!

11:45.760 --> 11:50.890
However, I hear you've lost quite a few wives and children...

11:52.560 --> 11:54.190
Well then, excuse me.

11:56.190 --> 11:57.980
How blasphemous of you.

11:58.690 --> 12:01.150
I cannot be held responsible for whatever may happen to you

12:01.150 --> 12:03.150
because you treated a fuda so poorly.

12:03.570 --> 12:04.860
Please leave.

12:05.070 --> 12:06.450
Very well.

12:10.240 --> 12:12.910
You are quite the curious one, sensei.

12:13.500 --> 12:15.370
You'll get your fingers burned for that.

12:18.670 --> 12:22.300
Kichibee-san, please stop this celebration!

12:23.460 --> 12:27.260
Umm... well, it's really dangerous!

12:27.470 --> 12:30.890
Never show your face here again!

12:52.160 --> 12:54.540
To think that it'd be useful at a time like this!

12:56.080 --> 12:57.750
Have you seen Yae-sama?

12:57.080 --> 12:58.920
Hey, what are you fussing about?

12:59.960 --> 13:02.880
Well... Yae-sama is nowhere to be found!

13:02.880 --> 13:04.750
What? The bride?

13:04.800 --> 13:06.420
Could she be in the bathroom or something?

13:06.420 --> 13:07.590
We checked there...

13:07.840 --> 13:09.470
Anyway, search for her!

13:09.760 --> 13:10.390
Yes, sir!

13:11.100 --> 13:12.760
They'll never find me here!

13:12.930 --> 13:16.640
But up here, I can't see what's going on inside at all.

13:22.900 --> 13:24.770
Yae-san?

13:31.410 --> 13:33.070
I won't hand him over to you!

13:36.330 --> 13:37.450
Yae-chan!

13:50.180 --> 13:51.130
Are you okay?

13:52.260 --> 13:54.180
Ogin-oneechan?

13:59.810 --> 14:00.890
Are you okay?

14:01.480 --> 14:03.900
Ogin-oneechan?

14:04.820 --> 14:06.520
You don't need to worry anymore.

14:06.730 --> 14:07.650
Where am I?

14:07.990 --> 14:09.820
What... happened... to me...?

14:10.240 --> 14:11.700
It's been a while.

14:15.090 --> 14:15.910
Yae!

14:20.020 --> 14:21.060
Are you okay?

14:21.820 --> 14:23.020
Somebody...

14:23.730 --> 14:26.490
The wind outside must have made her sick...

14:26.650 --> 14:28.530
Let's get you changed out of those.

14:28.570 --> 14:29.660
Come, quickly!

14:30.000 --> 14:30.820
But...

14:32.120 --> 14:33.450
I'm with you. You'll be fine.

14:34.120 --> 14:35.450
Ogin-oneechan...

14:35.830 --> 14:38.210
You haven't changed a bit since then.

14:39.080 --> 14:40.380
Ogin-oneechan...

14:49.010 --> 14:49.760
Idiot.

14:53.510 --> 14:54.930
Did you have to go this far?

14:58.440 --> 14:59.100
Why?

15:00.020 --> 15:01.810
Why did you do that to Yae?

15:02.150 --> 15:03.150
Because of you.

15:04.110 --> 15:05.860
You're the one who wanted it.

15:06.070 --> 15:07.030
I did?

15:08.200 --> 15:10.570
You thought that woman was in the way.

15:10.780 --> 15:11.620
I did not!

15:12.620 --> 15:14.200
Go away!

15:14.910 --> 15:16.040
Please!

15:20.460 --> 15:22.040
You must be tired, Yae.

15:22.280 --> 15:22.890
No...

15:23.880 --> 15:26.300
Now that you're pregnant, staying up longer would not be good.

15:26.460 --> 15:28.010
Go ahead and sleep.

15:28.340 --> 15:29.130
What about you?

15:29.470 --> 15:31.680
I'm going to keep company a little longer.

15:47.650 --> 15:48.940
Where did everyone go?

15:52.870 --> 15:56.330
Once Kichibee's chiid is born, Yanagiya's prosperity is assured.

15:56.700 --> 15:57.830
Indeed.

15:57.830 --> 15:59.750
His bride seems to have a good head on her shoulders, too.

15:59.750 --> 16:02.210
Shall we have Kichibee retire?

16:02.580 --> 16:03.540
Indeed.

16:04.540 --> 16:06.420
That man is too serious.

16:06.460 --> 16:09.170
He's not fit to be the owner of an inn.

16:09.800 --> 16:13.130
Let's have him retire right away and live in the annex,

16:13.180 --> 16:15.260
so that we don't have to look at his gloomy face anymore.

16:17.350 --> 16:18.720
Why?

16:19.140 --> 16:22.980
I've worked as hard as I could until now...

16:23.270 --> 16:27.570
But even so... the minute I have a kid, they're ready to throw me out.

16:29.240 --> 16:30.740
S-Somebody...

16:31.070 --> 16:32.490
It's just like I said.

16:33.360 --> 16:35.990
I'm your only ally.

16:37.120 --> 16:38.660
Yanagi Onna...

16:39.040 --> 16:42.160
Save... save me!

16:52.930 --> 16:56.510
I won't let you steal what's important to him.

17:01.310 --> 17:02.100
What?

17:08.230 --> 17:10.530
Oh no, I'm supposed to be keeping watch.

17:16.530 --> 17:17.740
At a time like this?

17:20.240 --> 17:21.200
Otoku?

17:21.870 --> 17:23.460
I've already killed you.

17:24.790 --> 17:26.080
You may have escaped death, but...

17:30.380 --> 17:31.300
What?

17:32.090 --> 17:35.470
You killed all of them like this, didn't you?

17:36.970 --> 17:37.890
You...

17:39.350 --> 17:41.470
I am the Yanagi Onna.

17:41.930 --> 17:42.770
What?

17:43.270 --> 17:45.440
You aren't a Yanagi Onna.

17:46.060 --> 17:48.230
That's right. Isn't it, Kichibee-san?

17:50.360 --> 17:52.110
That's... Ogin-san?

17:53.030 --> 17:55.570
And that's the Yanagi Onna?

17:56.570 --> 17:58.110
No, that's...

17:58.950 --> 18:00.450
N-No!

18:00.580 --> 18:01.280
I am...

18:02.950 --> 18:05.410
No... I am!

18:06.040 --> 18:08.500
The murders of those four wives...

18:08.500 --> 18:10.790
and the gruesome murders of their babies...

18:10.880 --> 18:12.170
That was all your doing.

18:12.210 --> 18:13.340
Not me!

18:13.550 --> 18:16.260
Save me! It's that woman! She acts on her own...

18:16.300 --> 18:17.300
That woman...

18:17.720 --> 18:19.140
Kichibee-san!

18:20.640 --> 18:22.560
I won't hand him over.

18:23.140 --> 18:26.560
He... belongs only to me.

18:26.980 --> 18:29.520
Only... only to me...

18:30.980 --> 18:34.070
All of it... was done by that woman!

18:34.110 --> 18:36.950
That's right. I'm the one who did it.

18:37.280 --> 18:39.070
For him.

18:39.530 --> 18:41.320
Save me...

18:41.580 --> 18:43.620
This house belongs to him.

18:44.120 --> 18:45.790
I won't hand it over to anyone.

18:45.910 --> 18:49.000
I'm not the one at fault! It's not my fault!

18:49.210 --> 18:51.880
Kichibee-san is the Yanagi Onna?

18:52.090 --> 18:54.880
It's not me... that woman did it!

18:55.380 --> 18:56.800
Yanagi Onna...

18:55.380 --> 18:57.000
I'm not the one at fault!

18:57.130 --> 19:02.760
That is another you; born of your weak heart.

18:57.430 --> 19:00.030
It's that woman who's at fault!

19:00.190 --> 19:02.030
It's not me!

19:04.560 --> 19:06.560
Sad, isnt it?

19:07.350 --> 19:09.640
If you insist on maintaining your own Way, then you will aggravate people,

19:09.650 --> 19:12.650
but if you stray from your ethics, then you will fall into depravity.

19:12.900 --> 19:15.230
Evil and ambition scatter into the darkness,

19:15.230 --> 19:17.900
and all that remains is a sad rumor among the townspeople.

19:18.900 --> 19:21.660
Your sins won't go away.

19:27.620 --> 19:29.080
It wasn't me...

19:30.120 --> 19:32.710
the Yanagi Onna did it... the Yanagi Onna did it!

19:34.300 --> 19:35.170
It's not me!

19:55.780 --> 19:57.860
The deed is done.

20:07.830 --> 20:09.960
Master! Master!

20:12.170 --> 20:13.210
Don't get any closer to it!

20:13.380 --> 20:15.460
It's a curse! A curse!

20:27.140 --> 20:29.640
How unfortunate for Kichibee-san,

20:29.640 --> 20:32.890
but at least Yanagiya is safe now.

20:33.520 --> 20:35.520
I'm so glad!

20:35.770 --> 20:37.820
With this, the eleventh master of the inn has been born!

20:39.400 --> 20:41.070
Glad, huh?

20:42.030 --> 20:46.370
It's your selfishness that drove Kichibee-san to his death.

20:47.620 --> 20:50.580
You guys are the real mononoke.

20:59.380 --> 21:00.130
Yae...

21:01.630 --> 21:03.970
you, at least, must become happy.

21:32.180 --> 21:35.710
Kyougokutei

21:45.800 --> 21:47.970
About that man named Momosuke,

21:49.350 --> 21:53.930
It's quite strange that he has twice witnessed your trickery.

21:54.100 --> 21:56.190
I-It's just a coincidence!

21:56.730 --> 22:01.190
Do you think that maybe he's come to know a little too much?

22:16.670 --> 22:22.760
Wind chimes whisper
soft and sweet

22:24.110 --> 22:30.200
Though there's not
a hint of a breeze

22:31.180 --> 22:36.950
Moonlight dancing
on the garden walk

22:36.990 --> 22:43.620
As it gently drifts
through the trees

22:44.990 --> 22:50.930
Romance takes flight
on this perfect night

22:50.970 --> 22:57.630
While all of the world
lays sleeping

22:58.470 --> 23:07.940
Find us here as we feel
the moment of love

23:09.250 --> 23:12.450
Draw near

23:12.720 --> 23:19.720
Dream, sleep,
with your hand in mine

23:19.760 --> 23:25.700
Underneath a blanket of stars

23:27.870 --> 23:33.140
Song birds singing
in a distant glade

23:33.180 --> 23:41.810
As we share
the warmth of the dawn

23:50.130 --> 23:52.510
Evil and ambition scatter into the darkness,

23:52.510 --> 23:55.550
and all that remains is a dubious rumor among the townsfolk.

23:56.470 --> 23:58.930
In the mountain's depths, there is a hunter named Yasaku.

24:00.020 --> 24:02.140
Killing beasts is Chikushoudou.

24:00.020 --> 24:02.140
[Note: Chikushoudou is the path of animality, which is one of the six paths of Buddhism.]

24:02.310 --> 24:04.520
[Note: Sesshoudou is the path of killing, which is one of the ten evils of buddhism.]

